WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
- You know how many 49-year-old men

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.990
do not believe in themselves?
- Yep.

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:04.050
- Most.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.840
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.323
You got your perspective.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.640
I just wanna be happy,
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.870
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.850
- Gary, I think one of
the things we wanna hit on

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.640
is women entrepreneurs

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.020
Angela and I have owned
our own business now

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.240
for seven years.
- Amazing.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.970
- We work together and
we are a partnership

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.133
and we actually still
really like each other.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.310
We actually like each other even more

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.550
than we did when we began.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.120
- That means you guys are communicating.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.426
- We are.
- Oh 100%.

00:00:32.426 --> 00:00:34.040
- I think we communicate more
than I sometimes communicate

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:34.873
with my husband.

00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:36.450
- That makes a lot of sense.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.363
- Her husband gets really jealous, too.

00:00:38.363 --> 00:00:39.780
(laughing)

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.466
- Because we spend a lot of time together.

00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:42.299
- It makes sense.
- Yeah,

00:00:42.299 --> 00:00:43.132
and you have to, right?

00:00:43.132 --> 00:00:45.100
- Yeah. You know, a lot of
people that are confused

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.780
about entrepreneurs, they don't realize

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.380
that the business is
the other family member.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.813
- Yeah, 100%.
- Oh, it's so true.

00:00:51.813 --> 00:00:52.646
- I mean, it just is.

00:00:52.646 --> 00:00:54.913
A business is another
child, another spouse.

00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:56.900
It's intense.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.340
It's the output of people's passion.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.623
I look at business as more like friends.

00:01:03.552 --> 00:01:04.385
You know, like you don't get to choose

00:01:04.385 --> 00:01:07.400
who you're born into
as parents or siblings

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.290
but you do pick your
friends and a lot of times

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.480
that's why those are the most
meaningful relationships.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.180
You do get to pick your business.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.260
- You do and you create
this culture, right?

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.300
And you create this family.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.740
Like we have our Theory Family

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.250
that is our staff, it's our
spouses, it's our coach.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.810
It's everybody and we have this culture

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.490
and it's our clientele.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.230
Like it's not just selling to us,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.830
it's creating this lifestyle
with people that we love.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.890
- Not only that, when you
then start breaking down

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.424
how many hours you work.
- It's not work.

00:01:37.424 --> 00:01:39.536
- [Woman] It's not work to us at all.

00:01:39.536 --> 00:01:41.210
- Listen, I get that and
that's why it's working.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.690
- Yeah.
- But, you start cutting down

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.610
how much time you work on your not work,

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.220
or your work, or your
business, or your product

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.410
and you start realizing
my god, my profession,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.110
my career, my passion, you know,

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.120
if you're lucky enough like you guys are,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.290
is the majority of what
I spend my time on.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.890
- Yes.
- Very true, very true.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.102
- I think that's why I'm so passionate

00:02:01.102 --> 00:02:03.450
about communicating my points of view

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.636
on what the internet has created.

00:02:05.636 --> 00:02:07.940
I mean, looking at the
five of us, none of us

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.040
were born into a world where
this much opportunity existed.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.370
Our parents and grandparents
did not have this opportunity.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.230
They just didn't.
- No.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.870
- The internet is like electricity.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.120
It's like running water and I don't think

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.870
we've understood that.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.320
Electricity and running water lead to like

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.890
better quality of life day-to-day.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.950
The internet leads to happiness

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:31.350
if you choose to harness it.
- Oh, 100%.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.650
- It's a big deal.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.760
- [Woman] It's so hard to teach

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.060
that you can be happy, right?

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.830
You can go outside of those restraints

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.050
that you have put on yourself.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.410
- Everybody was taught to go to school

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.880
and stay within a system.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:42.713
- [Woman] Or what about a woman?

00:02:42.713 --> 00:02:43.960
You were taught to be a mom, right?

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.150
And stay at home.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.690
That's a huge thing that we push back

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.640
in our small community
because Angela's a mom

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.867
and I'm not and I've
chosen to run the business

00:02:50.867 --> 00:02:52.090
and not have kids.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.767
She's chosen to be a working mom.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:57.000
- [Angela] But then I have
that, you know, struggle, right?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.230
- Yeah, and I think both of you

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.190
probably have that struggle.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.961
I think everybody has struggle, right?

00:03:00.961 --> 00:03:02.294
- [Angela] Yeah.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.280
- As soon as you were just saying that

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.089
I'm like oh, that's good.

00:03:06.089 --> 00:03:08.420
Why I said that's good in my head is

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.440
I'm a very big believer
that if you see anybody

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.790
in your circumstance succeed in happiness,

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:18.360
forget about money, well then you can too.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.860
You know, like if
there's anybody out there

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.690
who was born into two parents
that were addicted to heroin

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.980
and were never around and that person

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.950
went on to achieve
happiness then every child

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.500
who sees that person can point to that.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.640
I think it's very powerful
to be co-founders.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.950
One who does have a
family and one who doesn't

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.630
because your audience then
gets to see themselves

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.603
in one of you.
- That's very true.

00:03:42.603 --> 00:03:44.020
- I think that's incredible.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.310
- [Woman] So, Gary, our big question is

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:47.410
how do we get that out more?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.040
Our sort of story.
- Content.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.640
- [Woman] I think we
struggle every single day

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.100
with our business.
- Content.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.800
- But we do a ton of content.
- More.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.037
- [Woman] More.

00:03:55.037 --> 00:03:57.167
(laughing) We knew you were
going to say that, too.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.200
